---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About and sources" active="about">
  <style>
    .page { padding-top: 36px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; }
    h1 { margin: 0; font-size: 32px; }
    h2 { margin: 12px 0 0; font-size: 22px; }
    .src { padding: 20px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px; }
    .src p { margin: 0; }
    .notice { font-size: 13px; white-space: pre-wrap; background: var(--bg); border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px; margin-top: 6px; }
  </style>
  <div class="narrow page">
    <h1>About and sources</h1>
    <p style="margin:0;font-size:17px">This is a free, open website for reading and studying the Quran. It has no server and no database: a GitHub Action gathers open datasets, turns them into small JSON files, and GitHub Pages hosts the result. Your bookmarks and settings stay in your browser.</p>

    <h2>Sources and licences</h2>
    <div class="card src">
      <b>Quran text: Tanzil Project</b>
      <p>Uthmani text, version 1.1. Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 3.0. <a href="https://tanzil.net" rel="noopener">tanzil.net</a></p>
      <div class="notice">Tanzil Quran Text (Uthmani, Version 1.1)
Copyright (C) 2007-2026 Tanzil Project
License: Creative Commons Attribution 3.0

This copy of the Quran text is carefully produced, highly verified and continuously monitored by a group of specialists at Tanzil Project.

TERMS OF USE:
- Permission is granted to copy and distribute verbatim copies of this text, but CHANGING IT IS NOT ALLOWED.
- This Quran text can be used in any website or application, provided that its source (Tanzil Project) is clearly indicated, and a link is made to tanzil.net to enable users to keep track of changes.
- This copyright notice shall be included in all verbatim copies of the text, and shall be reproduced appropriately in all files derived from or containing substantial portion of this text.

Please check updates at: http://tanzil.net/updates/</div>
    </div>
    <div class="card src">
      <b>Morphology: Quranic Arabic Corpus</b>
      <p>Version 0.4, copyright (C) 2011 Kais Dukes. Licence: GNU General Public License. <a href="https://corpus.quran.com" rel="noopener">corpus.quran.com</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="card src">
      <b>Translations and metadata: AlQuran.cloud</b>
      <p>Translation text and mushaf page, juz and sajdah boundaries. <a href="https://alquran.cloud" rel="noopener">alquran.cloud</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="card src">
      <b>Recitations: EveryAyah</b>
      <p>Ayah-by-ayah audio, streamed directly. <a href="https://everyayah.com" rel="noopener">everyayah.com</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="card src">
      <b>Word by word: Quran Foundation</b>
      <p>Word meanings and transliteration, when enabled. <a href="https://quran.foundation" rel="noopener">quran.foundation</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="card src">
      <b>Mushaf page layout: Quranic Universal Library (QUL), Tarteel</b>
      <p>KFGQPC V2 layout, 604 pages of 15 lines (1421H Madani print), from <a href="https://qul.tarteel.ai" rel="noopener">qul.tarteel.ai</a>. Every line of the mushaf pages breaks where it does in print.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card src">
      <b>Quran font: King Fahd Glorious Quran Printing Complex</b>
      <p>KFGQPC HAFS Uthmanic Script, version 2.2, used unmodified under the Complex’s free end-user licence. To suit this font, a few marks are shown with the code points it uses for the same signs (for example the round sign over a silent letter); the Tanzil text itself is not changed.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card src">
      <b>Other fonts</b>
      <p>Amiri Quran (fallback) and IBM Plex Sans, via Google Fonts, under the SIL Open Font Licence.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:0">If you notice an error in any text, please report it to the original source so every app that uses it benefits.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
